@node LibreClaw Installation
@section Installation

@subsection Prerequisites

On Fedora:

@example
sudo dnf install \
    glib2-devel gobject-introspection-devel \
    libsoup3-devel json-glib-devel libyaml-devel \
    cmark-devel sqlite-devel libetpan-devel libpq-devel
@end example

On Debian/Ubuntu:

@example
sudo apt install \
    libglib2.0-dev libgirepository1.0-dev \
    libsoup-3.0-dev libjson-glib-dev libyaml-dev \
    libcmark-dev libsqlite3-dev libetpan-dev libpq-dev
@end example

@subsection Submodule

LibreClaw is @emph{not} a submodule of cmacs.  It is clawtilla's, and
cmacs builds that one copy, at @file{deps/clawtilla/deps/libreclaw}.

The two projects move together, so a second pin here would put two
versions of the same library into one binary---which is what the
static-library dedup rules in @file{src/Makefile.in} exist to survive,
and not a thing to add more of on purpose.  Clawtilla owns the pin:
@strong{bumping libreclaw means bumping clawtilla}.

@example
git submodule update --init deps/clawtilla
git -C deps/clawtilla submodule update --init --recursive deps/libreclaw
@end example

Nested submodules (@file{deps/ai-glib}, @file{deps/yaml-glib},
@file{deps/podomation} inside libreclaw) come along for the ride---though
cmacs overrides @code{AI_GLIB_DIR} so libreclaw compiles against cmacs's
canonical @file{deps/ai-glib} rather than building a second one.

@subsection Configure flag

@example
./configure \
    --with-cmacs-glib --with-cmacs-gi \
    --with-cmacs-podomation \
    --with-cmacs-libreclaw \
    @dots{} other flags @dots{}
make -j$(nproc)
@end example

@code{--with-cmacs-libreclaw} implies @code{--with-cmacs-podomation}
at runtime — libreclaw shares its PodEngine.

@subsection System vs bundled

Like other subsystems:

@itemize
@item
@code{--with-cmacs-libreclaw} — build from @file{deps/clawtilla/deps/libreclaw}
@item
@code{--with-cmacs-libreclaw=system} — link against
@code{libreclaw >= 0.21.0} via pkg-config (0.21.0 added the bridge
subsystem used by the remote mode; libdex-1 was also added to the
system-deps set at the same time)
@end itemize

The bundled path pulls in libreclaw's vendored ai-glib, yaml-glib,
and podomation submodules.  The dedup logic in
@file{src/Makefile.in} (@code{_libreclaw_strip}) strips yaml-glib
and podomation duplicates from libreclaw's archive before linking.

@subsection GIR / typelib

Starting with libreclaw 0.18.0, the build always produces
@file{Lc-1.0.gir} and @file{Lc-1.0.typelib} (unless @code{GIR=0}).
@code{make install} drops them into
@file{$(libdir)/girepository-1.0} and @file{$(datadir)/gir-1.0}.

For in-tree builds, set @env{GI_TYPELIB_PATH} to
@file{deps/clawtilla/deps/libreclaw/build/release} so cmacs-gi finds the typelib:

@example
export GI_TYPELIB_PATH=$PWD/deps/clawtilla/deps/libreclaw/build/release:$GI_TYPELIB_PATH
src/emacs
@end example
